      "gap": "Definitions and source variant not plainly supplied. The entry asserts that 'the cumulative conditional logarithmic score is -log m_n(x_{1:n})' (body 457-459) but defines only the expected logarithmic loss L_p(q) (body 446-450); the cumulative score is never defined in the entry or the annex (annex 576-578 only rewrites -log m_n as -sum_i log r_i). The cited source's form of this identity is not preserved or recorded: Kass and Raftery sec. 3.2 (held PDF p. 6, journal p. 777) define the logarithmic score with the opposite orientation, LS = sum_i log p_i(y_i), with log pr(D|H_k) = LS_k and log B_10 = LS_1 - LS_0. Under the source's definition the entry's displayed value has the wrong sign, and the entry gives no note of the convention change."
